// @expect-error Expected '->' after the switch labels, for example '1 -> handleOne()'
// @expect-error build failed with 1 problem
// A label list ends at 'default' or 'is', because neither can be a label and both begin an arm, so
// the comma in front of one separated arms rather than labels. That leaves the comma to the arm
// list and makes the missing thing this arm's body, which is one mistake and reads as one: without
// it the keyword was taken for a label and reported three times over.
main() -> int {
    int value = 1;
    long tag = switch (value) {
        1, default -> 0,
    };
    print("tag " + tag);
    return 0;
}
